Ethical Considerations
This study will be conducted in accordance with relevant ethical guidelines for research
involving human participants. Participation will be voluntary, and informed consent will
be obtained before data collection. Participants will be informed of the purpose of the
study, the procedures involved, and their right to withdraw at any time without penalty.
To protect privacy, all collected data will be anonymized before analysis, and personally
identifiable information will not be included in research outputs. The study will collect
interview responses, AI-generated feedback, questionnaire responses, and related
evaluation data solely for research purposes. The AI system will be used as a research
tool to generate and evaluate interview feedback, and all data will be stored securely and
accessed only by the researcher. Ethical approval and institutional requirements will be
followed prior to conducting the study.
Scope and Limitations
The scope of this research is limited to interview preparation within selected domains and
companies. While the system aims to simulate realistic interview scenarios, it may not
capture the full variability of real-world interviews. Furthermore, the evaluation is
conducted on a limited user group, which may affect the generalizability of the results.
The evaluation framework relies on AI-generated assessments and predefined rubrics,
which may not fully represent human judgments in all situations. Future work may
explore larger participant groups, multimodal analysis, and comparisons with expert
human evaluators to further validate the proposed framework.
